# Bio quiz content

Add topics and questions in the data files. Leave the runner files closed.

## New topic

Append to `QUIZ_SECTIONS` in that chapter's `*QuizData.js`:

```js
{ id: "active-transport", label: "Active transport", labelZh: "主動運輸" }
```

Then add questions whose `section` equals that `id`. Update the count string in `public/osmosis/quiz-hub.html`.

## New MCQ

Push onto the chapter array (`CELL_QUIZ`, `MEMBRANE_QUIZ`, `ENZYME_QUIZ`, or `FOOD_NUTRITION_QUIZ`):

```js
{
  id: "at-1",
  section: "active-transport",
  difficulty: "Foundation", // Foundation | Standard | Applied
  stem: "English stem",
  stemZh: "繁體中文題目",
  options: [
    { key: "A", text: "Option A", textZh: "選項甲" },
    { key: "B", text: "Option B" },
    { key: "C", text: "Option C" },
    { key: "D", text: "Option D" },
  ],
  answer: "B",
  hint: "Brief explanation",
}
```

`id` must be unique in that chapter. Optional `image: { src, alt, caption }` using a file already under `public/osmosis/assets/` (or a new image committed next to the existing ones).

T/F and fill-in: append in the matching `*QuizExercises.js` with the existing `tf()` / `fill()` helpers. Same `section` id.

## Remove a topic

Delete that section's questions from `*QuizData.js` and `*QuizExercises.js`, remove the `QUIZ_SECTIONS` row, then fix the hub count.

## Do not

Copy Chem `questions.json` shape (`ch`, `n`, string `options`). Do not rename an existing `id`. Do not change `quizId` (it lives in the runner).
